This is a precis of what I think jboskologists think about logic in Lojban,
or at least what I think that I think. :-)

Either the latter, or I'm not a jboskologist. :)



Existential import is required by quantifiers which do not allow 0 as a

possible value: specifically, "ro" and "su'o" have import, "no" and 
"me'iro"

do not.

In my view this should read: specifically, "su'o" and "me'iro"
have import, "ro" and "no" do not.

It is hard to interpret "less than all" as true when there
are none.

mu'o mi'e xorxes




